== the attribution, pure ==
a mostly slow window is dispersed, and the dispersion-only rule refuses it: true
its spread is its median over its floor: true
a quiet host admits it at its minimum: true
the admitted window keeps its dispersion and spread: true
a co-tenant keeps the refusal: true
no signal keeps the refusal: true
a uniformly delayed window under a co-tenant is admitted as before: true
a quiet host does not make an unresolved clock usable: true
the attribution policy is the CPU backends' and only theirs: true
== the host-load classification ==
a many-thread routine consuming the machine's busy time is quiet: true
residual load of several cores is a co-tenant: true
just under the bar is quiet and just over it a co-tenant: true
the allowance asks a short span for more evidence than a long one: true
the precise own time running ahead of the tick-sampled busy count is quiet: true
a counter that went backwards, a non-finite reading or an empty span is no signal: true
padding a short window does not dilute a co-tenant that ran only during it: true
a window longer than its span, or not positive, is no signal: true
the real counters resolve to a verdict over a 0.3 s span: true
== one timing call ==
isolated: the scripted window is dispersed with spread 3: true
isolated: a quiet host admits it at the floor: true
isolated: a co-tenant refuses it as contention: true
isolated: the dispersion-only policy refuses it and reads no load: true
isolated: the load span covers exactly the window's batches: true
queued: the scripted window is dispersed with spread 3: true
queued: a quiet host admits it at the floor: true
queued: a co-tenant refuses it as contention: true
queued: the dispersion-only policy refuses it and reads no load: true
queued: the load span covers exactly the window's batches: true
queued depth-1 reuse: the scripted window is dispersed with spread 3: true
queued depth-1 reuse: a quiet host admits it at the floor: true
queued depth-1 reuse: a co-tenant refuses it as contention: true
queued depth-1 reuse: the dispersion-only policy refuses it and reads no load: true
queued depth-1 reuse: the load span covers exactly the window's batches: true
the depth-1 shape reuses the calibration singles: true
the fast queued shape batches deeper than one: true
a short dispersed window reads once more after its wait and charges the span's foreign load to it: true
== an executed cc search ==
quiet: the search timed candidates and refused no window: true
quiet: every admitted window was dispersed: true
quiet: each one has a log line naming it: true
quiet: the winner's spread is recorded: true
quiet: the search committed a schedule entry: true
quiet: the second call replays it, with the stored spread: true
co-tenant: the windows are refused as contention: true
co-tenant: none of the search's cache operations stores a schedule: true
